cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software in your research, please cite it as below."
title: "diorthosis: compiling published critical editions into TEI and AI-ready Markdown"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Girardi
    given-names: Romain
    affiliation: "CEPAM UMR 7264, Université Côte d'Azur"
repository-code: "https://github.com/romain-girardi-eng/diorthosis"
version: "0.7.0"
date-released: 2026-08-04
license: MIT
keywords:
  - critical-edition
  - apparatus-criticus
  - TEI
  - digital-humanities
  - classics
  - textual-criticism
abstract: >-
  diorthosis compiles published critical editions (born-digital PDFs, or the
  ALTO/hOCR/PAGE-XML output of any OCR engine) into TEI P5 with the apparatus
  criticus split from the constituted text, parsed under explicit convention
  grammars, anchored to it by double-end-point attachment and preserved
  verbatim, plus a deterministic AI-ready Markdown view (md-ce/0.3) rendered
  from the same model. A whole-band convention gate refuses any apparatus the
  implemented grammars do not define, keeping its exact source slice with the
  gate's measured reason attached, so no structure is claimed beyond the
  evidence. Block-level provenance distinguishes decoded from OCR-generated
  text permanently.
